                <pb facs="0412" n="405" xml:id="pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9347: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-14T10:00:00+08:00">August 14, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 14—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>476. My 474, August 13, 10 p.m. Heavy artillery firing still continues same area
                    at intervals. So far as I am able to ascertain all Americans at Shanghai are
                    safe and have withdrawn from areas of firing.</p>
                <p>2. Chinese City Government functioning just outside of French Concession at
                    Fenglingchao. Sent to the Department, Nanking and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
